  "id": "EXAMPLE-001",
  "title": "Why your phone battery dies faster in the cold",
  "theme": "story",
  "script": "Ever notice your phone dies faster in winter? It's not broken. Inside the battery, tiny charged particles carry the power. When it's cold, they slow down, like people walking through thick mud. So the phone sees less energy and shuts down early. Warm it back up and most of that charge returns. The fix is simple: keep it in an inside pocket.",
  "emphasis": ["winter", "slow", "mud", "returns", "pocket"],
